ajv4l2 (26.09.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * HDMI output as a mirror of an SDI output: an hdmi file on every SDI
    output node puts that output's picture and eight audio channels on the
    KONA 5 HDMI connector, one output at a time; hdmi_sink and hdmi_edid
    tell the sink and its EDID.
  * The DMA segment length the card's descriptors take is declared: the
    DMA API debug checks flagged every 2 MiB segment of vb2-dma-sg.

 -- Max Lapshin <max@flussonic.com>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:49:10 +0000

ajv4l2 (26.09.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release. Capture and output nodes for every SDI connector of a
    KONA 5: picture, audio, ancillary data packets and per-frame metadata
    in one buffer by the common SDI frame contract (sdi_av.h, version 4)
    with the AJAV vendor block. Input detection, media controller, hwmon,
    sysfs counters and output settings (level A/B, reference). Verified
    against a DekTec card in both directions at 1080i50, 2160p25 over 6G
    and 2160p50 over 12G.

 -- Max Lapshin <max@flussonic.com>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 06:00:00 +0000
